        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.82,
          "end": 40.747,
          "en": "Now it'll be a very simple todo API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 45.29,
          "en": "And I noted everyone hates todos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.29,
          "end": 47.38,
          "en": "but I'm going to go with some todos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.38,
          "end": 50.7,
          "en": "because it's not so much about the fancy application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.7,
          "end": 53.6,
          "en": "but it's about the differences between node and Deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.6,
          "end": 57.55,
          "en": "And the easier the API is and the less amount of work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 57.55,
          "end": 58.99,
          "en": "we have to do there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 58.99,
          "end": 61.87,
          "en": "the easier it will be to grasp the differences",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 61.87,
          "end": 65.27,
          "en": "and to grasp Deno's core features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.27,
          "end": 68.14,
          "en": "So I have the todos.js file in the routes folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.14,
          "end": 69.85,
          "en": "I have the app.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.85,
          "end": 71.61,
          "en": "And now of course, in node's case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.61,
          "end": 74.55,
          "en": "I wanna use express.js here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 77.01,
          "en": "So therefore I'll navigate into the node folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.01,
          "end": 81.18,
          "en": "and run npm init to create a new package.json file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.18,
          "end": 83.71000000000001,
          "en": "where I'm going to confirm all the defaults,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.71000000000001,
          "end": 85.15,
          "en": "so that now in that folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.15,
          "end": 89.37,
          "en": "we can run npm install to install express.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.37,
          "end": 91.73,
          "en": "And I'll also install the body parser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 91.73,
          "end": 94.223,
          "en": "to parse incoming request bodies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.53999999999999,
          "end": 99.82,
          "en": "Now in app.js, we then require express.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.82,
          "end": 103.39,
          "en": "That's how we import in node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 103.39,
          "end": 107.08,
          "en": "We could also import with the modern import syntax,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.08,
          "end": 109.9,
          "en": "which I cover in the modern JavaScript module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.9,
          "end": 112,
          "en": "but I'll stick to this traditional approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 112,
          "end": 114.58,
          "en": "which you'll see in most projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.58,
          "end": 117.9,
          "en": "Also, I, again, disabled the Deno extension,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.9,
          "end": 121.41,
          "en": "so that I get good IDE support in node code?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.41,
          "end": 122.73,
          "en": "No, actually that's not the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 122.73,
          "end": 124.27,
          "en": "That's the express package, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 124.27,
          "end": 126.05,
          "en": "but we then create the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 126.05,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "That's what we do by calling express like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 132.85,
          "en": "And on that app, we then can call, listen, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.85,
          "end": 137.85,
          "en": "on port 3000 to start listening on that app server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 137.85,
          "end": 141.34,
          "en": "And now we can register some middleware in node express",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141.34,
          "end": 143.82999999999998,
          "en": "with the use method as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.82999999999998,
          "end": 146.72,
          "en": "Now, I will outsource some middleware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.72,
          "end": 148.89,
          "en": "into the todos.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.89,
          "end": 153.01,
          "en": "So here we again, import express by requiring express.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.29,
          "end": 158.24,
          "en": "And then here we get access to the router by extracting it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 158.24,
          "end": 160.723,
          "en": "from express.Router like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.63,
          "end": 165.92000000000002,
          "en": "And actually that should be lowercase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.92000000000002,
          "end": 167.06,
          "en": "because then on the router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.06,
          "end": 172.06,
          "en": "we can register various routes like a get route to /todos,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 172.21,
          "end": 174.2,
          "en": "which will get a middleware function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.2,
          "end": 178.6,
          "en": "with request, response, and next that should return todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.6,
          "end": 180.68,
          "en": "And by the way, if that's brand new to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 180.68,
          "end": 183.21,
          "en": "definitely go through the respective sections",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.21,
          "end": 186.83,
          "en": "in this course first, this is all node express knowledge",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.83,
          "end": 188.92,
          "en": "you gained throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 188.92,
          "end": 191.01,
          "en": "So we have this get route.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 191.01,
          "end": 193.3,
          "en": "We then have a post route to /todos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 193.3,
          "end": 196.603,
          "en": "to get a new todo, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 198.66,
          "end": 201.72,
          "en": "And we then also have a put route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.72,
          "end": 204.05,
          "en": "to replace a todo, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.05,
          "end": 209,
          "en": "Here, I also want to get the todoId as part of the URL",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 209,
          "end": 210.99,
          "en": "so that we can extract it from there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 210.99,
          "end": 215.49,
          "en": "and identify the fitting todo and update that accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.49,
          "end": 216.62,
          "en": "It's up to you, by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.62,
          "end": 220.13,
          "en": "if you wanna have a put or a patch route here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.13,
          "end": 223.74,
          "en": "And we also have to delete route to todos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.74,
          "end": 227.76,
          "en": "and then also some specific todoId, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 227.76,
          "end": 230.82,
          "en": "and then we'll have that middleware function here as well",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 230.82,
          "end": 235.82,
          "en": "to delete a todo, just like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.09,
          "end": 239.97,
          "en": "And ultimately, we export the router here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.97,
          "end": 244.97,
          "en": "so that in the app.js file, we can import the todo routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 248.71,
          "end": 253.71,
          "en": "by requiring ./routes/todos.js,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.15,
          "end": 258.7,
          "en": "without the extension actually just todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 258.7,
          "end": 259.88,
          "en": "This is how we import this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 259.88,
          "end": 262.48,
          "en": "and now we can use this as a middleware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 262.48,
          "end": 265.69,
          "en": "and we could also add some other middleware if we wanted to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 265.69,
          "end": 268.89300000000003,
          "en": "we can register any middleware whenever we want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 270.65,
          "end": 274.953,
          "en": "So here I could console.log some middleware",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 278.15,
          "end": 281.05,
          "en": "and I can always call next to proceed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.05,
          "end": 283.75,
          "en": "to the next middleware in line.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 283.75,
          "end": 287.11,
          "en": "So that's how we can do this in node express.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 287.11,
          "end": 289.36,
          "en": "Of course our logic is missing here though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 289.36,
          "end": 293.5,
          "en": "So to keep it simple, I'll just have a todos array up there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 293.5,
          "end": 295.54,
          "en": "which is a very simple array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.54,
          "end": 297.90999999999997,
          "en": "And when we get a get request,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 297.90999999999997,
          "end": 302.46,
          "en": "I just want to send back a response with some JSON data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 302.46,
          "end": 306.96,
          "en": "where I add a todos property, which holds the todos array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 306.96,
          "end": 309.71,
          "en": "So a very simple response.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 309.71,
          "end": 313.49,
          "en": "If we get a post request, I'll create a newTodo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 313.49,
          "end": 318.053,
          "en": "which is a JavaScript object that might have an id.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 319.84,
          "end": 324.31,
          "en": "That id could be the current date converted to an ISOString.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 324.31,
          "end": 326.26,
          "en": "And I have the todo text,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 326.26,
          "end": 329.16,
          "en": "which I expect to get from the request.body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 329.16,
          "end": 331.74,
          "en": "There, I expect to have a text field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 331.74,
          "end": 335.05,
          "en": "And in order to be able to extract that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 335.05,
          "end": 339.72,
          "en": "from the body, in app.js, I also want to import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 339.72,
          "end": 342.19,
          "en": "the body-parser by requiring it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 342.19,
          "end": 345.65999999999997,
          "en": "from the body-parser package, which we installed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 345.65999999999997,
          "end": 350.2,
          "en": "And I'll register the bodyParser.json middleware here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 350.2,
          "end": 352.69,
          "en": "And this will parse all incoming requests,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 352.69,
          "end": 354.83,
          "en": "check if they carry JSON data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 354.83,
          "end": 357.81,
          "en": "And if they do, the JSON data will be parsed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 357.81,
          "end": 361.04,
          "en": "and will be made available as a JavaScript object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 361.04,
          "end": 363.063,
          "en": "on the request.body field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 364.26,
          "end": 366.81,
          "en": "So we can create a newTodo then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 366.81,
          "end": 369.03,
          "en": "and we can then reach out to todos",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 369.03,
          "end": 371.693,
          "en": "and push the newTodo onto todos.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 375.58,
          "end": 377.46,
          "en": "By the way, if you followed along",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 377.46,
          "end": 379.49,
          "en": "with the TypeScript section in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 379.49,
          "end": 383.19,
          "en": "this API might look quite familiar to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 383.19,
          "end": 385.983,
          "en": "Now for updating a todo, we need to get that todoID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 386.95,
          "end": 388.85699999999997,
          "en": "I'll store it in a constant named tid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 390.06,
          "end": 392.403,
          "en": "And we get it from the request.params,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 393.45,
          "end": 395.86,
          "en": "and there we'll have a todoId param",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 395.86,
          "end": 397.86,
          "en": "because that's the name we picked here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 397.86,
          "end": 399.75,
          "en": "So we can extract it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 399.75,
          "end": 402.84000000000003,
          "en": "And now we need to find the index of the todo",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 402.84000000000003,
          "end": 404.43,
          "en": "in the todos array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 404.43,
          "end": 409.42,
          "en": "So todoIndex is todos, which is our array, findIndex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 409.42,
          "end": 413.21,
          "en": "and findIndex takes a function that executes for every todo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 413.21,
          "end": 415.94,
          "en": "So here we get every todo as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 415.94,
          "end": 418.61,
          "en": "and we wanna return true if the todo.id",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 418.61,
          "end": 420.463,
          "en": "is equal to the extracted tid.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 423.01,
          "end": 425.53,
          "en": "Then we know that's the to do we wanna update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 425.53,
